10.60.030
Fine schedule NOTICE OF VIOLATION.

When a vehicle is found to be in violation of this chapter a notice specifying the violation
and amount of the fine will be affixed to the vehicle, or sent to the address indicated by current
license plate registration records to the registered owner of the vehicle.
The notice of violation will also indicate the time and place of court appearance. The
violation(s) may be paid in the manner indicated on the notice in lieu of a court appearance. as
follows:
A.
Improper parking, including wrong side, blocking alley and blocked sidewalk
$ 10.00
B.
No parking zone
20.00
C.
Handicap parking only
100.00
D.
Illegal parking of semi Tractor/trucks
100.00
E.
Overstaying time limitation

First violation in a six month period: (Warning)
$ 0.00

Second in a six month period:
10.00

Third in a six month period:
20.00

Fourth and all subsequent in a six month period:
40.00

Fines will start again at $0.00 at the expiration of each six month period from the date of
the first violation. In the event automated enforcement is inoperable, the fine for overstaying
time will be fifteen dollars ($15.00) per violation.

10.60.040
Penalty FINE SCHEDULE.
Any such fine imposed pursuant to a notice of violation issued under Section 10.60.030
shall be determined by the municipal court, including any late fees, and shall be made
available to the general public in the form of a fine schedule.   In lieu of appearing in court
fines must be paid in the manner indicated within five week days. Should the fine not be paid in
the five day period, a late penalty will apply in the amount of four dollars. An additional four
dollars late penalty will apply for each violation unpaid past thirty (30) days. Violations that remain
unpaid past ten (10) days the vehicle may be towed and impounded until such time as all overdue
fines are paid, the vehicle may be booted, or a warrant or summons issued.

